<title>HONG KONG: Korea Long-Term to set $100 mln FRN.</title>
<headline>Korea Long-Term to set $100 mln FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Long Term Credit Bank has mandated ABN Amro Hoare Govett and Sakura Finance Asia to arrange a US$100 million floating rate note issue, bankers said.</p>
<p>They said the facility has a final maturity of 364 days.</p>
<p>Price talk is around 43 basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>The facility will be issued off a US$2 billion Medium Term Note Programme, bankers noted.</p>
<p>General syndication is tentatively scheduled to start in early May 1997.</p>
<p>--Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
